# The development platform's service accounts.
#
# Separate accounts rather than a shared one, mirroring production, because the
# point of having a development platform is to rehearse the real thing - and a
# dev instance where one account does everything rehearses a system that does
# not exist.
#
# Deliberately NOT members of haproxy-mgmt. The development worker must not
# reach production's engine, and the phase 4 gate is exactly that: dev cannot
# read or change production, or use production's keys.
#
# `u!` locks the password, and nologin because none of these ever logs in.
# Unlike the node accounts, no forced command runs through their shell.

u! haproxy-ui-dev-web - "HAProxy Manager dev web service" - /usr/sbin/nologin
u! haproxy-ui-dev-worker - "HAProxy Manager dev worker service" - /usr/sbin/nologin
u! haproxy-ui-dev-poller - "HAProxy Manager dev poller service" - /usr/sbin/nologin
